WEBVTT

00:13.013 --> 00:15.557
- I'm home.
- Oh, Yota!

00:16.516 --> 00:17.726
I'm sorry about earlier.

00:18.268 --> 00:19.102
Huh?

00:19.185 --> 00:22.063
You probably don't wanna be seen
talking to family in front of

00:22.147 --> 00:24.524
your friends.
I embarrassed you, didn't I?

00:26.693 --> 00:28.278
You're at that age... Oh, why'd I call out

00:28.361 --> 00:30.488
- No, it's totally fine.
- to you like that?

00:30.572 --> 00:31.823
I mean you're a teenager.

00:34.826 --> 00:36.036
Thank you for the meal.

00:37.162 --> 00:37.996
Vroom!

00:38.079 --> 00:38.997
Oh, hey there.

00:39.080 --> 00:42.250
Oh, don't hog him so much, Haruto!

00:42.333 --> 00:44.252
Can I possibly finish my food first?

00:44.335 --> 00:45.170
No, now!

00:45.253 --> 00:46.796
You're too loud!

00:46.880 --> 00:47.714
Ahhh.

00:48.882 --> 00:50.508
Would you knock it off, you two!

00:50.592 --> 00:51.426
RUMBLE RUMBLE

00:52.052 --> 00:54.345
Don't bother your brother while
he's eating!

00:54.429 --> 00:55.305
WHOOSH

00:57.057 --> 00:59.059
- Oof!
- Do the airplane thing again.

00:59.559 --> 01:00.393
Do it!

01:00.477 --> 01:02.812
- Daddy doesn't have anything left.
- Hey, hey, hey, hey.

01:02.896 --> 01:04.189
- Do it!
- You want me to switch?

01:04.272 --> 01:08.151
No, you don't have to do anything but
eat your dinner. Goodness.

01:08.234 --> 01:09.069
Oh, thank you.

01:12.822 --> 01:13.656
Hey! Hey!

01:15.033 --> 01:15.867
Daddy!

01:24.793 --> 01:25.960
All the noise...

01:26.628 --> 01:29.547
Keeps echoing around in my head non-stop.

01:29.631 --> 01:33.218
- Daddy, Daddy, Daddy!
- Listen to me you two!

01:36.304 --> 01:38.139
I have to make the noise stop.

01:39.349 --> 01:40.642
Or it'll swallow me up.

01:42.811 --> 01:43.645
Don't think.

01:45.647 --> 01:47.398
Don't think about anything.

01:52.529 --> 01:55.365
You see, in my family, I have a
younger sister and brother, and they're

01:55.448 --> 01:57.534
so pigheaded about getting
what they want.

01:57.617 --> 01:58.451
Mm-hm.

01:58.535 --> 02:01.329
The other day, when we were trying to
decide what to have for dinner, as

02:01.412 --> 02:04.624
soon as my sister said "pasta",
my brother simultaneously said "curry!"

02:04.707 --> 02:06.167
Neither of them would give in.

02:06.251 --> 02:07.085
So, I had to-

02:07.168 --> 02:10.046
My younger brother and sister are
still little, so it can get pretty

02:10.130 --> 02:11.631
noisy at home.

02:12.507 --> 02:14.259
Have you been up here all this time?

02:14.342 --> 02:16.469
Yup. Mmm.

02:17.887 --> 02:21.349
You know, daydreaming sounds even better.

02:21.933 --> 02:24.060
The more I think about what he said...

02:25.728 --> 02:28.648
The more everything else he's said
makes so much sense.

02:30.692 --> 02:32.610
But even if I'm right about all of it...

02:33.820 --> 02:36.489
Is it something I should even be getting
involved in?

02:37.991 --> 02:40.535
But if someone insists that they're okay...

02:41.411 --> 02:42.829
Then I should believe them.

02:44.664 --> 02:47.000
And just stay out of their business, right?

04:13.378 --> 04:15.713
THE RAMPARTS OF ICE

04:20.134 --> 04:23.930
Loneliness and Solitude

04:24.013 --> 04:25.223
201 YUKI

04:25.306 --> 04:26.849
Koyuki, listen...

04:27.392 --> 04:29.936
Me and your father are divorcing.

04:32.772 --> 04:34.357
- Do you like my apron?
- I knew my parents weren't super

04:34.440 --> 04:35.275
You look adorable, dear.

04:35.358 --> 04:37.610
Lovey-dovey like those couples you
see on TV.

04:38.736 --> 04:41.739
- And that they sometimes argued when
- I'm working myself to the bone all day,

04:41.823 --> 04:42.657
I wasn't around or they thought

04:42.740 --> 04:44.158
- I couldn't hear.
- every day.

04:44.242 --> 04:47.120
I knew all of that. I had no illusions.

04:48.913 --> 04:53.918
But... even then, I was super
close with Mom.

04:54.877 --> 04:57.880
And I felt secure knowing Dad loved me
and was there for me.

04:59.048 --> 05:02.260
I'm pretty sure I was the only
thing keeping them together.

05:04.095 --> 05:06.014
So I thought it would all be okay.

05:07.807 --> 05:09.600
Would Dad be just fine without me?

05:10.351 --> 05:11.269
YUKI

05:11.352 --> 05:12.270
HIKAWA

05:13.062 --> 05:14.981
Like I never even mattered to him?

05:20.194 --> 05:22.447
Ew, her water bottle is so lame,
isn't it?

05:22.530 --> 05:24.615
Oh my gosh, stop, Manatsu!

05:26.284 --> 05:27.702
I didn't fit in at school.

05:28.453 --> 05:32.290
I felt like I didn't belong anywhere,
really, no matter where I was.

05:33.458 --> 05:37.962
Tell me, Koyun, what it is you don't
like about Igarashi?

05:38.046 --> 05:39.213
There's probably a lot.

05:40.423 --> 05:43.801
I felt so isolated with no one I
could share my feelings with.

05:44.886 --> 05:45.803
And this fear...

05:47.055 --> 05:50.433
This voice that wouldn't leave me
alone said, "no one cares whether

05:50.516 --> 05:52.810
you're around or not."

05:53.895 --> 05:56.731
Eventually, I started to believe it.

05:57.482 --> 05:59.067
And it broke my heart.

06:01.402 --> 06:03.821
CLUB WITHDRAWAL FORM

06:09.410 --> 06:10.870
Back then, I...

06:12.163 --> 06:14.415
I felt lonelier when I was with someone.

06:19.921 --> 06:21.923
GRADE 1 CLASS 2

06:22.423 --> 06:25.093
WHEW... WHEW...

06:25.176 --> 06:27.595
Our circumstances are completely
different.

06:27.678 --> 06:30.181
- Yota isn't me.
- What time is your club over today?

06:30.264 --> 06:34.560
What feels right for me may be completely
different than what's right for him.

06:35.853 --> 06:38.481
Still... I know how he feels.

06:39.273 --> 06:40.608
- Send!
- SEND

06:41.317 --> 06:42.360
That loneliness...

06:43.319 --> 06:46.948
The kind you experience when you're
with others yet still feel so alone.

06:48.241 --> 06:49.075
Hm?

06:50.701 --> 06:51.869
Oh, Koyun.

06:51.953 --> 06:53.871
- KOYUKI: ABOUT WHAT TIME DOES YOUR CLUB
- Probably...

06:53.955 --> 06:57.417
- END TODAY? PROBABLY... A...
- Around when we're all-

06:57.500 --> 06:58.543
Hm?

07:00.378 --> 07:02.713
Agh! Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, your
phone!

07:03.381 --> 07:05.466
Ah! Whew! Close one.

07:06.467 --> 07:09.512
ABOUT WHAT TIME DOES YOUR CLUB END TODAY?
PROBABLY AN UPRISING

07:09.595 --> 07:11.597
Oh, uh, sorry. I appreciate it.

07:13.182 --> 07:14.100
I saw it.

07:16.602 --> 07:18.521
Probably an uprising.

07:19.355 --> 07:20.690
What does this mean?

07:22.233 --> 07:23.985
- Huh?
- Probably around when we're all leaving.

07:24.068 --> 07:25.278
Sorry, typo! LOL

07:26.529 --> 07:27.697
- Whew!
- HEH

07:28.197 --> 07:30.533
BLAZING CHINESE GYOSHO

07:31.325 --> 07:34.537
And then, before I could fix it,
I dropped my phone and ended up

07:34.620 --> 07:36.122
sending it instead.

07:37.498 --> 07:39.834
I was like, oh my gosh, that's a
heck of a typo.

07:39.917 --> 07:40.918
What can I say?

07:44.088 --> 07:44.922
You grandpa.

07:45.006 --> 07:47.258
Oh, so I've gone from "dad" to "grandpa"
now.

07:50.928 --> 07:52.513
Sorry for dragging you along.

07:52.597 --> 07:53.639
It's fine.

07:57.185 --> 07:58.019
Mm.

07:59.562 --> 08:00.396
Um...

08:01.105 --> 08:01.939
So my...

08:03.232 --> 08:04.442
My parents are divorced.

08:05.443 --> 08:06.277
Huh?

08:09.697 --> 08:11.657
I'm often alone when I get home.

08:13.242 --> 08:15.912
So if you're free, even if it's just
once in a while...

08:18.122 --> 08:21.667
I'd really like it if we could maybe hang
out after school.

08:26.214 --> 08:27.048
It'd be nice.

08:31.344 --> 08:32.887
You're such a kind person.

08:33.721 --> 08:35.139
Huh? N- No way!

08:35.223 --> 08:37.808
I'm judgy and moody and get mad
super easily.

08:37.892 --> 08:39.227
No you're not.

08:42.313 --> 08:43.231
You're very kind.

08:43.940 --> 08:45.066
At least to me.

08:46.567 --> 08:47.401
Hm.

08:49.153 --> 08:49.987
Sorry.

08:51.405 --> 08:54.492
But can I share with you for just a sec?

08:55.576 --> 08:56.410
Mm-hm.

09:03.584 --> 09:08.005
A little after my mom died, Dad just, he
suddenly got super busy.

09:08.714 --> 09:11.217
He couldn't make it to any school events.

09:12.343 --> 09:14.762
NOTICE OF CLASS OBSERVATION

09:15.388 --> 09:19.141
I tried not to let it bother me too much
on Bring Your Parent to Class days

09:19.225 --> 09:20.268
FIDGETY

09:24.689 --> 09:25.523
And then...

09:26.148 --> 09:28.234
Hi Yota, it's nice to meet you.

09:28.985 --> 09:30.152
You're so tall.

09:30.653 --> 09:31.862
Yota, meet Akari.

09:32.989 --> 09:36.492
Dad introduced me to the woman I now call
Mom.

09:37.702 --> 09:39.954
Uh. Sorry! He's just shy around people.

09:40.037 --> 09:41.664
Yota, c'mon she doesn't bite.

09:41.747 --> 09:43.791
Uh. Um, can we, um...

09:44.750 --> 09:48.045
And Mom, well, she's been super nice
to me.

09:55.428 --> 09:56.262
But...

09:58.055 --> 10:00.558
Akari! I got paternity leave!

10:01.100 --> 10:02.059
Ah, really!

10:02.143 --> 10:03.686
- Mm-hm!
- I'm so happy.

10:03.769 --> 10:06.022
- They finally approved it.
- Thank goodness.

10:06.105 --> 10:07.148
Sometimes I wonder.

10:08.316 --> 10:09.150
Ooh, yummy!

10:09.233 --> 10:11.402
- See? I knew you'd like it.
- Is it good?

10:11.485 --> 10:13.487
If I even exist to them.

10:15.156 --> 10:21.412
I feel like I'm the only one in the
family who just doesn't belong.

10:24.373 --> 10:26.292
I know I'm being really self-centered.

10:27.293 --> 10:29.545
But the thought won't leave me alone.

10:31.631 --> 10:32.882
I'm just running from it.

10:39.221 --> 10:43.434
Yota, you shouldn't beat yourself
up for how you feel or what you think.

10:44.226 --> 10:46.145
I know how he feels so much it hurts.

10:47.313 --> 10:49.607
Don't judge yourself for feeling what
you feel.

10:49.690 --> 10:51.400
It will just makes you feel worse.

10:52.735 --> 10:55.071
Because the more you judge and blame
yourself...

10:55.780 --> 10:58.908
You just hate yourself that much
more, right?

10:59.408 --> 11:02.620
Even if you run away from your
circumstances, you can't run away

11:02.703 --> 11:03.621
from yourself.

11:06.082 --> 11:07.792
You're amazing. You know that?

11:08.292 --> 11:09.335
Huh?

11:10.169 --> 11:11.087
You really see me.

11:22.515 --> 11:23.891
Huh? Wait, are you crying?

11:25.059 --> 11:25.893
Oh.

11:25.976 --> 11:27.395
- SHARP
- Don't worry about it.

11:27.478 --> 11:31.315
It's like a glitch that happens whenever
emotions get too big for me to process.

11:31.399 --> 11:33.109
- What?
- Yeah, happens all the time.

11:33.192 --> 11:34.235
Huh?

11:35.611 --> 11:37.905
I was jealous of Yota all this time.

11:38.489 --> 11:42.326
He was a different gender, height, had a
very different personality from me.

11:43.828 --> 11:47.832
I figured his kindness was a byproduct of
his strength and composure.

11:47.915 --> 11:48.833
Just who he was.

11:50.710 --> 11:53.295
But it came from pushing things down
or giving up.

11:54.755 --> 11:57.216
And that's... That's so sad.

11:59.802 --> 12:00.636
Yota.

12:01.512 --> 12:03.097
You don't have to be nice all the time.

12:03.180 --> 12:04.223
Hm?

12:05.266 --> 12:07.476
It's okay to feel what you wanna feel.

12:13.774 --> 12:15.568
SIGH

12:15.651 --> 12:16.485
Hm?

12:17.236 --> 12:18.654
Thanks for letting me vent.

12:19.363 --> 12:21.115
Sorry, I hope I wasn't too weird.

12:21.699 --> 12:23.826
Not at all. You're fine.

12:25.327 --> 12:28.205
All that stuff I told you, I've never
shared with anyone.

12:28.998 --> 12:31.917
To be honest, I wouldn't even have
shared this with Minato.

12:32.001 --> 12:33.002
I'm surprised.

12:33.794 --> 12:35.796
You really care for Amamiya, don't you?

12:37.339 --> 12:38.174
No way.

12:38.883 --> 12:39.717
Okay, sure.

12:41.427 --> 12:44.472
If you're fine with me, then I'm happy to
listen.

12:45.848 --> 12:51.979
If you hold it in too much, then your
heart will just get all covered in soot.

12:52.521 --> 12:53.397
- In soot?
- Mm-hm.

12:53.481 --> 12:54.315
In soot.

12:55.691 --> 12:57.777
As it builds up, it makes everything
harder.

12:57.860 --> 13:00.237
And you can't see things clearly anymore.

13:03.699 --> 13:04.533
Hmm.

13:04.617 --> 13:05.451
I see.

13:05.951 --> 13:07.077
Sounds about right.

13:08.871 --> 13:09.705
Mmm.

13:11.540 --> 13:12.374
Uhh.

13:14.168 --> 13:15.002
Mmm.

13:19.465 --> 13:20.382
What should I do?

13:20.883 --> 13:21.801
Huh?

13:23.344 --> 13:24.178
Koyun.

13:24.887 --> 13:25.721
I, um...

13:35.564 --> 13:36.398
Well, I...

13:38.651 --> 13:39.527
You see...

13:40.402 --> 13:41.237
I like...

13:43.697 --> 13:44.532
Huh?

13:53.791 --> 13:54.750
You see...

13:54.834 --> 13:55.918
I like...

13:58.712 --> 13:59.547
Huh?

14:02.550 --> 14:04.552
I like... Miki.

14:12.434 --> 14:14.270
What? What? What?

14:14.353 --> 14:15.896
PANIC

14:15.980 --> 14:17.565
FLUSTER FLUSTER

14:18.065 --> 14:19.024
What?

14:24.196 --> 14:25.030
Yeah, it's both.

14:27.324 --> 14:28.200
No way.

14:29.243 --> 14:30.744
I- I didn't see this coming!

14:30.828 --> 14:32.746
You seem so chill all the time!

14:33.581 --> 14:36.000
Oh, well, yeah, I'm really not.

14:36.917 --> 14:40.421
If you haven't noticed, I'm always
a total mess whenever Miki's around.

14:40.504 --> 14:41.547
Really?

14:42.172 --> 14:43.424
But I've never seen...

14:49.138 --> 14:49.972
Never mind.

14:50.890 --> 14:53.809
Minato figured it out a long time ago.

14:54.351 --> 14:57.229
IT'S NOT THE CASE
WAIT, WAIT

14:57.313 --> 15:00.316
- He must feel embarrassed.
- I keep denying it cause it annoys me.

15:00.399 --> 15:02.318
Whoa. What Is this feeling?

15:02.943 --> 15:04.194
I'm super happy!

15:06.071 --> 15:08.574
Maybe I don't even know who the real me
is.

15:08.657 --> 15:11.452
Or what my real feelings even are.

15:11.535 --> 15:12.411
GRR!

15:12.494 --> 15:15.289
Like, don't fantasize about who
you think I am and then get mad when

15:15.372 --> 15:18.876
Like, don't fantasize about who
you think I am and then get mad when

15:18.959 --> 15:19.793
Well, Miki...

15:19.877 --> 15:21.837
There's someone who likes you
just the way you are.

15:21.921 --> 15:23.631
And... He's such a wonderful person.

15:28.218 --> 15:29.970
(BURSTING-WITH-JOY DANCE)

15:30.054 --> 15:34.058
- You wanna date Miki, huh?
- Koyun, why are you suddenly acting weird?

15:34.141 --> 15:34.975
So, Yota.

15:35.059 --> 15:35.893
GIDDY

15:35.976 --> 15:37.269
Sorry, I'm just happy.

15:37.353 --> 15:38.479
Oh, but...

15:43.192 --> 15:44.652
How does Miki feel about him?

15:46.904 --> 15:48.864
I haven't thought that far.

15:50.366 --> 15:52.993
Honestly, I don't really plan
on telling her.

15:54.453 --> 15:55.955
I just like her, is all.

15:56.455 --> 15:57.748
Let's leave it at that.

15:58.958 --> 16:00.000
Her friendship...

16:00.084 --> 16:01.460
Means the world to me.

16:03.128 --> 16:06.382
And I know she doesn't see me the
same way, and honestly I'm okay

16:06.465 --> 16:07.716
with that.

16:09.134 --> 16:09.969
But then...

16:11.220 --> 16:14.890
Keeping this secret, I'm starting to
feel like I'm deceiving her

16:15.975 --> 16:19.019
I feel like I should apologize for liking
her.

16:19.520 --> 16:20.521
GASP

16:20.604 --> 16:22.314
I told you, don't blame yourself!

16:22.398 --> 16:23.399
The soot!

16:27.486 --> 16:29.571
Let's keep this conversation between us.

16:29.655 --> 16:30.781
I won't say a word.

16:31.281 --> 16:33.033
I'm really rooting for you, Yota.

16:33.534 --> 16:35.411
Just don't be too obvious around her.

16:36.870 --> 16:37.705
I'll try.

16:39.832 --> 16:40.666
Hm.

16:41.750 --> 16:42.793
It feels like a thumb.

16:42.876 --> 16:43.711
It's my pinky.

16:45.462 --> 16:49.258
You know, I'm really glad I became
friends with you.

16:53.470 --> 16:54.304
I am too.

16:57.433 --> 16:58.475
Yota! Welcome back!

16:59.643 --> 17:00.477
I'm home.

17:01.395 --> 17:02.813
STARE

17:03.313 --> 17:05.065
Did you stop somewhere on your way?

17:05.149 --> 17:05.983
EEK

17:06.066 --> 17:07.317
Did I come home too late?

17:08.485 --> 17:10.195
Yeah. With a friend.

17:10.696 --> 17:11.822
Oh, I knew it!

17:12.573 --> 17:16.285
You looked cheerful, so I thought maybe
something good might've happened.

17:17.327 --> 17:18.162
Huh?

17:18.662 --> 17:20.164
- Big brother!
- Big brother!

17:20.247 --> 17:21.540
Oh, come on!

17:22.791 --> 17:24.501
Can we dry our hair first, please?

17:24.585 --> 17:25.461
My goodness.

17:25.961 --> 17:27.337
But no, it's not fair.

17:27.421 --> 17:29.590
You always go straight to your room.

17:29.673 --> 17:30.716
Yeah.

17:30.799 --> 17:32.092
That's why we came to get you!

17:32.176 --> 17:33.343
Big bro, big bro, big bro.

17:33.427 --> 17:35.179
Go ahead and dry your hair. I'll wait
for you.

17:35.262 --> 17:36.096
Let's play!

17:36.180 --> 17:37.014
- Really?
- Really?

17:37.097 --> 17:38.015
Yeah!

17:38.098 --> 17:38.932
- Yay!
- Yay!

17:39.016 --> 17:39.850
- Ah!
- Jeez.

17:41.727 --> 17:42.978
Oh. Yota.

17:43.062 --> 17:44.354
There's ice cream in the freezer.

17:44.438 --> 17:45.481
The fancy kind.

17:46.190 --> 17:48.233
Only after he finishes his dinner.

17:48.317 --> 17:50.235
HMPH!

17:52.529 --> 17:56.784
Without even trying, everyone's
kindness is warming my heart.

17:59.661 --> 18:03.123
Why did I ever believe I didn't belong
here?

18:04.541 --> 18:05.375
Soot.

18:07.628 --> 18:08.712
So that's it.

18:09.630 --> 18:11.840
I never knew what it was before.

18:14.384 --> 18:16.512
I can't even remember the last time...

18:18.305 --> 18:19.556
I had a night this quiet.

18:23.977 --> 18:25.646
Did you sleep well last night?

18:25.729 --> 18:27.106
Yeah, very well.

18:27.731 --> 18:28.565
Good.

18:30.109 --> 18:30.943
What the...

18:31.985 --> 18:33.904
Oh, hey. You get something to drink?

18:33.987 --> 18:35.072
Uh-huh.

18:35.572 --> 18:36.406
Hey, Amamiya.

18:37.074 --> 18:37.950
It's been awhile.

18:39.743 --> 18:40.869
Uh, yeah, it sure has.

18:42.412 --> 18:43.247
Oh, great!

18:43.330 --> 18:44.164
- Hm?
- Hm?

18:44.248 --> 18:46.333
- The three of you are here together!
- Huh?

18:46.416 --> 18:49.586
- Jeez, she's got so many snacks.
- Jeez, she's got so many snacks.

18:49.670 --> 18:51.755
Having bread from the school store for
lunch too?

18:51.839 --> 18:53.090
Yeah, silly me.

18:53.173 --> 18:55.843
I forgot to grab my lunch on the
way out this morning.

18:55.926 --> 18:56.844
That's not good.

18:56.927 --> 18:57.886
Wait!

18:57.970 --> 18:58.929
There were buns left?

18:59.012 --> 19:00.514
Yeah. You can have it.

19:00.597 --> 19:02.224
No, I'll pay for it.

19:02.307 --> 19:03.142
How much?

19:04.017 --> 19:05.561
UNEASY

19:09.148 --> 19:09.982
Hmm.

19:11.525 --> 19:13.026
It's fine. You can have it.

19:13.110 --> 19:15.154
No, I wanna pay for it.

19:15.237 --> 19:16.113
Fine, ten yen.

19:16.196 --> 19:17.114
That can't be right.

19:17.197 --> 19:18.323
Let's trade one.

19:19.616 --> 19:20.450
Mm?

19:21.160 --> 19:22.035
Amamiya.

19:23.579 --> 19:25.581
So, what'd you do over winter break?

19:26.582 --> 19:28.041
She initiated a conversation.

19:29.168 --> 19:32.671
Just, uh, uh. mostly doing club
activities.

19:33.630 --> 19:36.008
And sometimes I hung out with my
classmates.

19:36.592 --> 19:38.177
And I walked my, uh, dog.

19:39.011 --> 19:39.845
A dog?

19:39.928 --> 19:41.096
FUZZY

19:42.139 --> 19:42.973
And I, uh...

19:44.141 --> 19:45.350
When I talk to her...

19:46.393 --> 19:49.313
No matter how hard I try, I can never say
the right thing.

19:50.355 --> 19:52.316
I don't know what to do.

19:53.650 --> 19:55.903
- By the way...
- Hm?

19:55.986 --> 19:58.071
- I'd really love to know the name.
- Huh?

19:58.155 --> 19:59.615
- My name?
- No.

19:59.698 --> 20:01.909
- Your dog's.
- Oh.

20:03.035 --> 20:04.953
Because I'm pretty sure you're Minato.

20:08.290 --> 20:09.124
It's Ponta.

20:10.000 --> 20:10.834
Huh?

20:11.335 --> 20:12.461
Oh, no, I meant the dog!

20:12.544 --> 20:14.546
- PONTA AMAMIYA PONTA
- I'm not Ponta, clearly!

20:14.630 --> 20:16.131
Wait, what am I even saying?

20:16.882 --> 20:18.717
- HEH
- Huh?

20:21.261 --> 20:22.262
Wow, I guess you're...

20:23.305 --> 20:24.932
- Ponta!
- Yeah, yeah.

20:25.432 --> 20:27.017
Go ahead, laugh it up.

20:28.310 --> 20:29.144
Sorry.

20:30.687 --> 20:33.273
Sweet red beans are clearly your
favorite, huh?

20:33.774 --> 20:34.983
Heck, yeah!

20:35.067 --> 20:36.610
I can't get enough of 'em!

20:36.693 --> 20:37.527
Right, Koyu-

20:38.028 --> 20:39.112
Is Ponta doing well?

20:39.613 --> 20:40.447
- Mm-hm.
- Wait,

20:40.530 --> 20:41.990
I take tons of pictures.

20:42.074 --> 20:44.368
- Ooh, I wanna see.
- Well, what's going on here?

20:44.451 --> 20:46.078
- Am I...
- Koyun...

20:48.830 --> 20:50.332
- Wha-
- What the heck?

20:51.541 --> 20:54.044
I've got lots of pent-up energy.

20:54.127 --> 20:55.254
What'd ya do that for?

20:55.337 --> 20:56.296
You scare me.

20:59.091 --> 20:59.925
Jeez.

21:00.008 --> 21:01.760
- I'm sorry.
- You're being too good of a wing

21:01.843 --> 21:03.303
- Eh, it's fine.
- woman there.

21:04.429 --> 21:05.264
Oh, gosh. Sorry.

21:05.347 --> 21:06.723
SMILE GUARD SMILE GUARD ALPHA

21:06.807 --> 21:08.767
Hey, I told you, stop making that face!

21:10.018 --> 21:10.852
Sorry, sorry.

21:11.603 --> 21:12.938
Huh? What's this?

21:13.605 --> 21:14.898
Are those two...

21:16.608 --> 21:20.195
- Their chemistry is off the charts!
- Their chemistry is off the charts!

21:20.737 --> 21:22.155
Well, I'm gonna go now.

21:22.656 --> 21:23.949
Eating in again?

21:25.158 --> 21:25.993
Yeah.

21:26.493 --> 21:27.327
Eating in where?

21:27.411 --> 21:28.578
THE SCHOOL NURSE NORIKO

21:28.662 --> 21:30.914
I said the nurse's office isn't
a food court!

21:31.832 --> 21:32.666
Well, see ya.

21:33.750 --> 21:34.584
Yeah, later!

21:39.381 --> 21:41.800
I can't totally say for sure yet,
but two of my favorite people in

21:41.883 --> 21:42.718
the whole world might be falling for each
other.

21:42.801 --> 21:45.220
The whole world might be falling for each
other.

21:47.014 --> 21:50.726
Oh my gosh, why does that make me so
freaking excited?!

21:52.019 --> 21:55.439
Hey, look, I- I know it's still a
long way off, but d'you guys wanna

21:55.522 --> 21:58.317
study together for final exams again?

22:03.113 --> 22:03.947
- Sure.
- Sure.

22:04.031 --> 22:04.865
Awesome!

22:05.824 --> 22:08.577
And I'll be playing the role of Cupid
for them!

22:11.163 --> 22:14.041
- Wait, is that Miki?
- Alright, I'm gonna study my butt off!

22:14.124 --> 22:17.836
The guys she's with.
That's clearly Hino and Amamiya, right?

22:19.796 --> 22:23.800
Guys, has Miki always been like that?
